      "writtenOn": "2024-05-24T16:18:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This won\u0027t do what it looks like. The underlying integer type of `enum pd_dual_role_states` is almost certainly unsigned. This assignment will probably assign it the maximum value, not corresponding to any enum value. If you compare it to -1 later, it will be unequal.\n\nThe appropriate default here should probably be `PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON`. If we have need to vary the default, it should probably be encoded in the devicetree. I can imagine doing that for something like honeybuns. If possible, I\u0027d like to avoid giving this enum some meaningless \"invalid\" value that all its users would then need to account for.",
      "revId": "eea4f5baba4084c629fcf05169b567c66f6973c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
